  "description": "The Straight Net is a vertical rope net held in an upright frame, finished in New Black and Horizon Teal. Children climb the net face, swing a leg over the top and come down the other side. A rope net moves as they climb, so each step trains balance and grip together. It is a simple piece that works well for a school or society that wants to add climbing without giving up much ground. The safe play area is 10' x 5'2\". Many buyers place it beside a slide or swing set to give children a short climbing station between rides. Galvanised pipe and play rope come with our 3-year warranty. Ask us how it fits alongside your existing equipment.",
